'''Imroosians''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that existed within [[the galaxy]] from the [[Volcano|volcanic]] [[planet]] [[Imroosia]]. Imroosians developed flinty, chalk-like skin,<ref name="Official Guide" /> cracked like dried out [[desert]] ground,<ref name="Padawan">[[Padawan (novel)|''Padawan'']]</ref> to adapt to their heated climate and were [[hair]]less.<ref name="Official Guide" />

During the [[High Republic Era]], [[Archivist]] [[Ru-Ru]] was an Imroosian serving the [[Jedi Order]] at the [[Jedi temple (Banchii)|temple]] on [[Banchii]].<ref name="Edge of Balance 1">[[The High Republic: The Edge of Balance, Vol. 1|''The High Republic: The Edge of Balance'', Vol. 1]]</ref> Another notable Imroosian was [[Margo]], who served as [[Dryden Vos]]' concierge aboard his [[yacht]], the ''[[First Light]]'' during the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Mem]] was a young<ref name="Padawan" /> Imroosian<ref name="Kiersten White">{{Threads|username=authorkierstenwhite|name=[[Kiersten White]]|url=post/DVnQeOLE8Og|quote=Correct on Mem and Zae-Brii! Jarper and Tumber are Lepi. (Lop & Ochō is one of my favorite episodes of Visions!)|date=2026-03-08|archivefile=File:KierstenWhite-PadawanSpecies-Threads.png}}</ref> who lived on the [[planet]] [[Lenahra]] during the late [[Republic Era]].<ref name="Padawan" /> Also during the Imperial Era, a young Imroosian named [[Agira]] served the [[House of Organa]] as the [[handmaiden]] of [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia]].<ref name="Part I">{{Kenobi|Part I}}</ref>

{{Species-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The Imroosians were developed for the [[2018]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|''Star Wars'' Anthology]] film ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'' from reused concept art of [[Qi'ra]], from when she was originally intended to be an alien.<ref name="Art of Solo">''[[The Art of Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

